{"changes":[{"target":"M2","current_line":"Built for developers: launch payments fast with our APIs, docs and sandbox.","type":"replace","change":"For marketplace and gig-app engineering leads: \"Build your own core payment flow, like paying your sitters, in our sandbox over a weekend, before you decide.\" Offer it as a guided step early in the evaluation, not just as a feature on a list.","evidence":["E18","E19","E25"],"why":"The docs and sandbox drew the strongest reaction, and the deal turned when a customer engineer built a working sitter payment flow over a weekend, after which Daniel 'stopped saying \"if\"'.","strength":"Test this"},{"target":"M11","current_line":"Onboard, verify and pay out to sellers worldwide, in their local currency.","type":"replace","change":"For gig and service apps where buyers don't call themselves a 'marketplace': \"Payments shouldn't be a team. Onboard, verify and pay your sitters locally in every country you launch, and stop babysitting payments.\" Swap in the prospect's own word for its workers (sitters, walkers, cleaners). Only add 'paid by Friday' once we have confirmed what payout timing we can promise.","evidence":["E36","E37","E41","E20","E3","E38"],"why":"The onboarding, identity and local payout capabilities landed, but the customer describes the job as 'sitter pay' and the pain as labour ('Payments shouldn't be a team', 'stop babysitting this', two engineers on upkeep), not as 'marketplace payouts'.","strength":"Test this"},{"target":null,"current_line":null,"type":"add","change":"For buyers switching from Braintree: add a 'What you keep when you switch' proof point that covers PayPal, Venmo and saved cards, plus a named, size-matched card-migration reference to use instead of generic customer stories (M8). Do not publish it until product confirms the Venmo answer and the PayPal coexistence details.","evidence":["E13","E32","E28","E29"],"why":"After the Braintree call the customer's main worry became 'do we lose PayPal, do we lose Venmo, what happens to the saved cards' and 'who's done this at our size', and we had no crisp Venmo answer and only deferred PayPal to implementation.","strength":"Test this"},{"target":"M4","current_line":"Customers see an average uplift in authorization rates with Authorization Boost and Adaptive Acceptance.","type":"drop","change":"Stop leading with the authorization-rate uplift for low-ticket marketplace and gig-app buyers. Use that slot for the sandbox build and the sitter onboarding, verification and local payout flow.","evidence":["E21","E23"],"why":"The acceptance-rate slide met silence, and the buyer dismissed it with his own numbers: 'our average booking is 38 dollars, I'm not losing sleep over auth rates.'","strength":"Test this"}],"no_change_reason":null}
